  tuple.reserve(values_tensor.size());

  // Create copy for insertion into Staging Area
  Tensor key(*key_tensor);

  // Add all values to the tuple
  for (const auto& value : values_tensor) {
    tuple.push_back(value);
  }

  // Store the tuple in the map
  OP_REQUIRES_OK(ctx, map->put(&key, indices_tensor, &tuple));
}
```

By using `reserve`, we ensure that the vector has enough space to hold all the elements without needing to reallocate memory, thus preventing buffer overflows.

